] ], processEscapes: true } }); </script> <script src='https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.4/latest.js?config=TeX-MML-AM_CHTML' async></script> <!-- end custom head snippets --> <!-- Global site tag (gtag.js) - Google Analytics --> <script async src=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-XXS8QXKDVG\"></script> <script> window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || []; function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);} gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', 'G-XXS8QXKDVG'); </script></head><body> <!--[if lt IE 9]><div class=\"notice--danger align-center\" style=\"margin: 0;\">You are using an <strong>outdated</strong> browser. Please <a href=\"http://browsehappy.com/\">upgrade your browser</a> to improve your experience.</div><![endif]--><div class=\"masthead\"><div class=\"masthead__inner-wrap\"><div class=\"masthead__menu\"><nav id=\"site-nav\" class=\"greedy-nav\"> <button><div class=\"navicon\"></div></button><ul class=\"visible-links\"><li class=\"masthead__menu-item masthead__menu-item--lg\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/\"><h1>Jamie Haddock</h1></a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/research/\">Research</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/publications/\">Publications</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/people/\">People</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/teaching/\">Teaching</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/code/\">Code</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/resources/\">Resources</a></li><li class=\"masthead__menu-item\"><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/personal/\">Personal</a></li></ul><ul class=\"hidden-links hidden\"></ul></nav></div></div></div><div id=\"main\" role=\"main\"><div class=\"sidebar sticky\"><div itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\"><div class=\"author__avatar\"> <a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io\"><img src=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/images/jamie.jpg\" class=\"author__avatar\" alt=\"Jamie Haddock\"></a></div><div class=\"author__content\"><h3 class=\"author__name\">Jamie Haddock</h3><p class=\"author__bio\"><b>Associate Professor</b><br>Department of Mathematics<br>Harvey Mudd College</p></div><div class=\"author__urls-wrapper\"> <button class=\"btn btn--inverse\">Follow</button><ul class=\"author__urls social-icons\"><li><i class=\"fa fa-fw fa-map-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Los Angeles, CA</li><li><i class=\"fa fa-fw fa-map-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> HMC Shanahan Center 2408</li><li><a href=\"mailto:jhaddock@g.hmc.edu\"><i class=\"fas fa-fw fa-envelope\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Email</a></li><li><a href=\"https://github.com/jamiehadd\"><i class=\"fab fa-fw fa-github\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Github</a></li><li><a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ONLOj-oAAAAJ&hl=en\"><i class=\"fas fa-fw fa-graduation-cap\"></i> Google Scholar</a></li><li><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1449-2574\"><i class=\"ai ai-orcid-square ai-fw\"></i> ORCID</a></li><li><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/files/HaddockCV.pdf\"><i class=\"fas fa-fw fa-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> CV</a></li><li><a href=\"https://forms.gle/Yg2yyT9RStNktkns5\"><i class=\"fas fa-fw fa-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Letter of Rec Form</a></li><!--<li><link href=\"https://assets.calendly.com/assets/external/widget.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\"> <script src=\"https://assets.calendly.com/assets/external/widget.js\" type=\"text/javascript\" async></script> <a href=\"\" onclick=\"Calendly.initPopupWidget({url: 'https://calendly.com/jamie-haddock'});return false;\"><i class=\"fas fa-fw fa-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Calendly</a></li>--></ul></div></div></div><div class=\"archive\"><h1 class=\"page__title\">Research</h1><script type='text/javascript'>//<![CDATA[ $(window).load(function(){ //when the page has loaded, run this function $(document).read(function () { //hide all sections tagged with the class \"section\" by default $('.section').hide(); //when an h4 element is clicked $('h4').click(function () { //add the class \"open\" (which changes the bg image to minus) $(this).toggleClass(\"open\"); //proceed to the next style and and make the hidden element //visible; or if it's shown, make it hidden $(this).next().toggle(); }); //end toggle }); //end ready });//]]> </script> <script type=\"text/javascript\"> function help_click(div, txt) { if (div.innerHTML == \"\") div.innerHTML = \"<br/> \" + txt; else div.innerHTML = \"\"; } </script><p><figure style=\"float: left; margin-right:50px; width:35%\"><img src=\"../images/Kacz.gif\"></figure><h2>Randomized iterative methods for large linear systems</h2>Solving large systems of linear equations and inequalities efficiently and effectively is one of the most common and foundational problems encountered in the data-rich sciences. One pillar of my research is developing iterative projection techniques for solving systems of such large scale that the problem-defining data cannot be held entirely in computer memory. My research has analyzed <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SclGSdwB7M4\"><i>Kaczmarz</i> methods</a> for a variety of problems, such as systems of linear inequalities, graph-defined systems, or noisy and corrupted systems of equations. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help270, \"<span><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/1912.03544\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Greed Works: An Improved Analysis of Sampling Kaczmarz-Motzkin</a> <br>(J. Haddock, A. Ma; SIMODS 2021) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2009.08089\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Quantile-based Iterative Methods for Corrupted Systems of Linear Equations</a> <br>(J. Haddock, D. Needell, E. Rebrova, W. Swartworth; SIMAX 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/1605.01418\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">A Sampling Kaczmarz-Motzkin Algorithm for Linear Feasibility</a> <br>(J.A. De Loera, J. Haddock, D. Needell; SISC 2017) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.03126\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Motzkins Method for Inconsistent Linear Systems</a> <br>(J. Haddock, D. Needell; BIT 2019) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.08114\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Randomized Projection Methods for Linear Systems with Arbitrarily Large Sparse Corruptions</a> <br>(J. Haddock, D. Needell; SISC 2018) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14609\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Paving the Way for Consensus: Convergence of Block Gossip Algorithms</a> <br>(J. Haddock, B. Jarman, C. Yap; IEEE TranIT 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07987\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Subsampled Quantile Randomized Kaczmarz</a> <br>(J. Haddock, A. Ma, E. Rebrova; Allerton 2023) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.10635\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Application of Block Kaczmarz Methods in Matrix Factorization</a> <br>(E. Chau, J. Haddock; SIURO 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Randomized Iterative Methods for Tensor Regression Under the t-product</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; Proc. WiSDM 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19874\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Quantile Randomized Kaczmarz for Linear Systems with Time-Varying Noise and Corruption</a> <br>(N. Coria, J. Haddock, J. Pacheco; 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.12021\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Block Matrix and Tensor Randomized Kaczmarz Methods for Linear Feasibility Problems</a> <br>(M. Zhang, J. Haddock, D. Needell; La Matematica 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.10583\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Randomized Kaczmarz methods for t-product tensor linear systems with factorized operators</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; BIT 2025) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.19155\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Block Gauss-Seidel methods for t-product tensor regression</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; NUMA 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.18190\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Quantile-Based Randomized Kaczmarz for Corrupted Tensor Linear Systems</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.20877\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Beyond Expectation: Concentration Inequalities for Randomized Iterative Methods</a> <br>(T. Anderson, M. Collins, J. Haddock, J. Lok, E. Rebrova; 2024)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"../slides/IterativeProjectionMethods.pdf\">Slides</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yaz7X2Xz4FE\">Video</a> ]<div id=\"help270\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: right; margin-left:50px; width:35%\"><img src=\"../images/Wolfe.gif\"></figure><h2>Combinatorial methods for constrained convex optimization</h2>Many iterative methods for convex optimization are numerical and convergent in nature, however, for select problems, there are common combinatorial (finite) methods. Wolfe's method is a finite algorithm for computing the projection onto a convex polytope, and its complexity was unknown since the introduction of the method in the 1970s; with collaborators, I showed that this method has exponential behavior in the worst case. Recently, I have been considering the Hanson-Lawson method for nonnegative least-squares. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help271, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02608\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">The Minimum Euclidean-Norm Point on a Convex Polytope: Wolfes Combinatorial Algorithm is Exponential</a> <br>(J.A. De Loera, J. Haddock, L. Rademacher; SIAM Computing 2019) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02608\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">The Minimum Euclidean-Norm Point on a Convex Polytope: Wolfes Combinatorial Algorithm is Exponential</a> <br>(J.A. De Loera, J. Haddock, L. Rademacher; Proc. STOC 2018)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"../slides/wolfe.pdf\">Slides</a> ]<div id=\"help271\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: left; margin-right:50px; width:35%\"><img src=\"../images/qmu_reconstruction.gif\"></figure><h2>Matrix factorization and tensor decomposition for topic modeling</h2>There is currently an unprecedented demand for interpretable methods to study large-scale, multi-modal tensor data. and represented well by a tensor. My research develops matrix and tensor decomposition models for learning the latent topics in the data while respecting the natural multi-modal structure of the data, incorporates flexible supervision information, and identifies hierarchical topic structure. We design and analyze efficient methods for training these models. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help272, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Quantile Multiplicative Updates for Corruption-Robust Nonnegative Matrix Factorization</a> <br>(Z. Collins, J. Haddock, T. Headley, L. Wang; SampTA 2025) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.18190\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Quantile-Based Randomized Kaczmarz for Corrupted Tensor Linear Systems</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.19155\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Block Gauss-Seidel methods for t-product tensor regression</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; NUMA 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.10583\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Randomized Kaczmarz methods for t-product tensor linear systems with factorized operators</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; BIT 2025) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Randomized Iterative Methods for Tensor Regression Under the t-product</a> <br>(A. Castillo, J. Haddock, I. Hartsock, P. Hoyos, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. R. Larripa, D. Needell, S. Suryanarayanan, K. Yacoubou-Djima; Proc. WiSDM 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2109.14820\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">A Generalized Hierarchical Nonnegative Tensor Decomposition</a> <br>(J. Vendrow, J. Haddock, D. Needell; ICASSP 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.02415\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Automatic Infectious Disease Classification Analysis with Concept Discovery</a> <br>(E. Sizikova, J. Vendrow, X. Cao, R. Grotheer, J. Haddock, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, T. Merkh, R. W. M. A. Madushani, K. Moise, A. Ulichney, H. V. Vo, C. Wang, M. Coffee, K. Leonard, D. Needell; ML4H 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://github.com/jvendrow/Neural-NNCPD\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Neural Nonnegative CP Decomposition for Hierarchical Tensor Analysis</a> <br>(J. Vendrow, J. Haddock, D. Needell; Proc. ACSSC 2021) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2010.07956\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Semi-supervised Nonnegative Matrix Factorization for Document Classification</a> <br>(M. Ahn, R. Grotheer, J. Haddock, L. Kassab, A Kryshchenko, K. Leonard, S. Li, A. Madushani, T. Merkh, D. Needell, E. Sizikova, C. Wang; Proc. ACSSC 2021) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.11365\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On a Guided Nonnegative Matrix Factorization</a> <br>(J. Vendrow, J. Haddock, E. Rebrova, D. Needell; Proc. ICASSP 2021) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2001.00631\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Dynamic Topic Modeling with Nonnegative Tensor Decomposition</a> <br>(M. Ahn, N. Eikmeier, J. Haddock, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. Leonard, D. Needell, A. Mudiyanselage, E. Sizikova, C. Wang; Proc. WiSDM 2019) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.00058\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Neural Nonnegative Matrix Factorization for Hierarchical Multilayer Topic Modeling</a> <br>(J. Haddock, T. Will, J. Vendrow, R. Zhang, D. Molitor, D. Needell, E. Sadovnik; extended abstract in Proc. CAMSAP 2019, Samp. Theory, Sig. Process., and Data Anal.) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.00631\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Dynamic Topic Modeling with Nonnegative Tensor Decomposition</a> <br>(M. Ahn, N. Eikmeier, J. Haddock, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, K. Leonard, D. Needell, A. Mudiyanselage, E. Sizikova, C. Wang; Proc. WiSDM 2019) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.10635\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">On Application of Block Kaczmarz Methods in Matrix Factorization</a> <br>(E. Chau, J. Haddock; SIURO 2020)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"../slides/tensor_talk.pdf\">Slides</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"https://hmc.mediasite.com/mediasite/Channel/hmc-stauffer-lecture-series-2022su/watch/b8a730fbcaf14b1d9b51dcd7175f9e011d\">Video</a> ]<div id=\"help272\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: right; margin-left:50px; width:25%\"><img src=\"../images/ranking.png\"></figure><h2>Network consensus and ranking</h2>Consensus and ranking problems can be understood as learning values for each node of a graph which respect some pairwise measurements (defining the edges of the graph). One can utilize tools from numerical linear algebra, combinatorial linear algebra, and the analysis of iterative techniques for linear systems to design and analyze methods for solving these problems. In particular, my research has focused on gossip methods for the average consensus problem, and recently has developed these types of methods for the ranking problem. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help273, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14609\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Paving the Way for Consensus: Convergence of Block Gossip Algorithms</a> <br>(J. Haddock, B. Jarman, C. Yap; IEEE TranIT 2022)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"../slides/ConsensusandNLAConnections.pdf\">Slides</a> ]<div id=\"help273\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: left; margin-right:50px; width:30%\"><img src=\"../images/cs.png\"></figure><h2>Methods in compressive sensing</h2>Compressive sensing techniques have revolutionized sensing and sampling, with applications in image reconstruction, hyper spectral imaging, wireless communications, and analog to digital conversion. Meanwhile, complex data-gathering devices have been developed, leading to problem instances so large that they cannot be stored or solved in conventional computers. My research has developed and analyzed asynchronous parallel sparse recovery methods for such problem, as well as learning models for selecting classical CS methods. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help274, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9048787\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Convergence of Iterative Hard Thresholding Variants with Application to Asynchronous Parallel Methods for Sparse Recovery</a> <br>(J. Haddock, D. Needell, N. Rahnavard, A. Zaeemzadeh; Proc. ACSSC 2019) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8645176\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">A Bayesian Approach for Asynchronous Parallel Sparse Recovery</a> <br>(A. Zaeemzadeh, J. Haddock, N. Rahnavard, D. Needell; Proc. ACSSC 2018) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/1905.13404\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Data-driven Algorithm Selection in Optimization and Signal Processing</a> <br>(J.A. De Loera, J. Haddock, A. Ma, D. Needell; Ann. Math. Artif. Intel. 2020)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ]<div id=\"help274\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: right; margin-left:50px; width:35%\"><img src=\"../images/echocardiograms.png\"></figure><h2>Data science applications in medicine</h2>I have been fortunate to be part of wonderful collaborations applying data scientific, mathematical, and statistical approaches to medically relevant data from various application partners. With Homeboy Industries, we performed thorough statistical tests analyzing data regarding side effects from tattoo removal. With LymeDisease.org, we performed various analyses on large-scale survey data from Lyme patients. My grant NSF DMS #2211318 funded a collaboration with the UCLA-Harbor Medical Center Department of Cardiology. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help275, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.02626\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">The text2term tool to map free-text descriptions of biomedical terms to ontologies</a> <br>(R. S. Gonçalves, J. Payne, A. Tan, C. Benitez, J. Haddock, R. Gentleman; Database 2024) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.02415\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Automatic Infectious Disease Classification Analysis with Concept Discovery</a> <br>(E. Sizikova, J. Vendrow, X. Cao, R. Grotheer, J. Haddock, L. Kassab, A. Kryshchenko, T. Merkh, R. W. M. A. Madushani, K. Moise, A. Ulichney, H. V. Vo, C. Wang, M. Coffee, K. Leonard, D. Needell; ML4H 2022) <br><br><a href=\\\"http://arxiv.org/abs/2009.09087\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Feature Selection on Lyme Disease Patient Survey Data</a> <br>(J. Vendrow, J. Haddock, D. Needell, L. Johnson; Algorithms 2020) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-9032/8/4/383\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Antibiotic treatment response in persistent Lyme disease: Why do some patients improve while others do not?</a> <br>(L. Johnson, M. Shapiro, R. Stricker, J. Vendrow, J. Haddock, D. Needell; Healthcare 2020) <br><br><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.09065\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Statistical Learning for Best Practices in Tattoo Removal</a> <br>(R. Yim, J. Haddock, D. Needell; SIURO 2022)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ]<div id=\"help275\"></div></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: left; margin-right:50px; width:18%\"><img src=\"../images/comm_detect.png\"></figure><h2>Community detection on graphs and hypergraphs</h2>Detecting latent community structure amonst entities with pairwise (or group-wise) relationships, e.g., graphs and hypergraphs, is a fundamental and widely-applicable task. With my collaborators, I have been investigating efficient spectral methods for detecting communities in various stochastic graph and hypergraph models, and thresholds for detectability using these techniques. I additionally consider provable matrix and tensor decomposition techniques for this task. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help276, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.13586\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Nonbacktracking spectral clustering of nonuniform hypergraphs</a> <br>(P. Chodrow, N. Eikmeier, J. Haddock; SIMODS 2023)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ] &nbsp; &nbsp; [ <a href=\"../slides/hypergraphcommdetection.pdf\">Slides</a> ]<div id=\"help276\"></div></p></p><!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --> <!-- %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% --><p><figure style=\"float: right; margin-left:50px; width:35%\"><img src=\"../images/zf_wagonwheel1.png\"></figure><h2>Eigenvalue problems in combinatorial linear algebra and zero-forcing</h2>Combinatorial linear algebra and combinatorial inverse problems find application in many areas, including in engineering design. My research has considered combinatorial inverse problems, including understanding the minimum number of eigenvalues of certain graph-structured matrices. This problem is related to zero-forcing, a dynamic graph process in which nodes of a specific color force the color change of their neighbors. We have also considered a probabilistic zero-forcing measure on graphs. <br>[ <a onclick='help_click(help277, \"<span><a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.12899\\\" target= \\\"_blank\\\">Zero forcing with random sets</a> <br>(B. Curtis, L. Gan, J. Haddock, R. Lawrence, S. Spiro; Discrete Mathematics 2024)</span>\")' href=\"javascript:;\">Publications</a> ]<div id=\"help277\"></div></p></p><br>Note: The lovely gif associated with \"Randomized iterative methods for large linear systems\" is due to my exceptional student Hannah Kaufman! This is a visualization of the Kaczmarz method. The gif associated with \"Combinatorial methods for constrained convex optimization\" is a 3D visualization of an exponential example for Wolfe's method, a combinatorial method for finding the point in a polytope nearest to the origin. The gif associated with \"Matrix factorization and tensor decomposition for topic modeling\" is due to my excellent student Tyler Headley. This is a visualization of an NMF method resolving an image over iterations of a method designed to avoid and remove the effect of corruption to a given dataset!</div></div><div class=\"page__footer\"><footer> <!-- start custom footer snippets --> <a href=\"/sitemap/\">Sitemap</a> <!-- end custom footer snippets --><div class=\"page__footer-follow\"><ul class=\"social-icons\"><li><strong>Follow:</strong></li><li><a href=\"http://github.com/jamiehadd\"><i class=\"fab fa-github\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> GitHub</a></li><li><a href=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/feed.xml\"><i class=\"fa fa-fw fa-rss-square\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Feed</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"page__footer-copyright\">&copy; 2026 Jamie Haddock. Powered by <a href=\"http://jekyllrb.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jekyll</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://github.com/academicpages/academicpages.github.io\">AcademicPages</a>, a fork of <a href=\"https://mademistakes.com/work/minimal-mistakes-jekyll-theme/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Minimal Mistakes</a>.</div></footer></div><script src=\"https://jamiehadd.github.io/assets/js/main.min.js\"></script> <script> (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i['GoogleAnalyticsObject']=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){ (i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o), m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m) })(window,document,'script','//www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js','ga'); ga('create', '', 'auto'); ga('send', 'pageview'); </script></body></html>\n"
